                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]200 character summary[/h1]\nBombfest is an amazing little brawler where you have to throw bombs at your friends in order to knock them off the level. It is local only but a whole lot of fun You can even customize your character.\n\n[h1]Gamemodes [b]7/10[/b][/h1]\nYou can only play the game locally with up to 4 players, There is no online, You can add bots, but the real fun is in playing ths game with your friends, It has very simple controls it is just dive/roll and pickup/throw so even non gamers can easily jump in without getting too confused. It only has 1 gamemode but it is fun for the whole family.\n\n[h1]Gameplay [b]9/10[/b][/h1]\nThe gameplay is very chaotic, Throwing bombs, diving away from the danger, Props that fly everywhere due to the explosions, Near misses, Insane explosions that blow you out of the map, or just amazing trickshots that you somehow survive. It really creates a lot of \"wow did you see that?!?\" moments. It is also very well suited for kids.\n\nYou will unlock new things after every game, Things like New levels, Outfits, Accessories, New Bombs, But also game modifiers which can drastically change the game, Like higher jumps, force rolling, big head mode, and a few more to spice things up, I personally prefer the stock game without the timer, But it is nice to be able to change the rules, You can even make it rain nukes right from the start. You can set the number of rounds, Set which bombs fall into the arena and how often, You can adjust the timer, bots, which levels are added to the pool, Almost everything can be adjusted. \n\nThere are dozens of outfits and accesories you can mix and match to create your own unique character, There are also a whopping 14 different bombs, Some are sticky, Bouncy, Slidy, Some go up in the air or implode instead of explode. Some explode directly, there are mines and many many more, It is a blast to play this game, It creates some very tense and funny moments. The game can get a little stale after an hour or so. But it is just as fun next time you play it.\n\n[h1]Aesthetics [b]9/10[/b][/h1]\nYou play as little wooden dolls and the arenas are all set in and around the house, On a table, on a carpet, in the sink or on a playmat. It looks very playful inviting, is easy to play and encourages rivalries. \n\n[h1]Performance [b]8/10[/b][/h1]\nThe performance is great, It is locked to your framerate but tt runs at a stable 120fps all the time. I had absolutely no issues, crashes or any other bad behavior.\n\n[h1]Replayability [b]9/10[/b][/h1]\nIt is just so much fun if you have multiple controllers, You will unlock everything pretty early on, and there is not much more to do than throwing bombs at eachother, but it surely is a lot of fun.\n\n[h1]Improvements[/h1]\nI would love to see more gamemodes, games with a prop that must be forced out of the arena, Maybe protect your own and destroy enemy castles or something like that. Maybe even team modes. I would also love to see more different arenas, I think there is a good mix, but more levels would be very cool.\n\n[h1]Conclusion [b]9/10[/b][/h1]\nOverall Bombfest is an amazing little brawler It is perfect fun for short bursts of gameplay, I really enjoy it and I believe it is among the best local brawlers on Steam. If you have multiple controllers, Not having Bombfest is just a waste, If you like local brawlers you should definitely own this game. \n\n[quote][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/35216846/][h1]Follow my Curator Page for more Reviews like this[/h1][/url][/quote]\n\n[h1]Game Info[/h1]\n[table]\n[tr]\n\t[td]# of players[/td]\n\t[td]Up to 4 players locally[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Steam Cloud Save[/td]\n\t[td]Not Available[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Controller Support[/td]\n\t[td]Yes, Xbox One Bluetooth Working[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Achievements[/td]\n\t[td]Don't work on Linux[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]FPS on Ultra 1080P[/td]\n\t[td]Locked to framerate[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Launch Command[/td]\n\t[td]gamemoderun %command%[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Installed Size[/td]\n\t[td]350MB[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Issues[/td]\n\t[td]Achievements not working[/td]\n[/tr]\n[/table]\n\n[h1]Operating System & Hardware[/h1]\n[table]\n[tr]\n\t[td]OS[/td]\n\t[td]Arch Linux[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]Kernel[/td]\n\t[td]5.4.8[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]DE[/td]\n\t[td]Gnome 3.34.2[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]CPU[/td]\n\t[td]Intel I7-6800K Hexa Core @ 4.2 Ghz[/td]\n[/tr]\n[tr]\n\t[td]GPU[/td]\n\t[td]Nvidia Geforce GTX 1080 (Nvidia 440.44 Drivers)[/td]\n[/tr]\n[/table]",
